  "goodToKnow": "Die Sintflut is the biblical Flood, survived by Noah in the Arche. Sint- is an old prefix meaning great or all-encompassing; folk etymology later linked it to Sünde (sin), giving the variant Sündflut. Nach mir die Sintflut (after me, the deluge) means not caring about consequences. It also means a deluge: eine Sintflut von E-Mails. Plural: die Sintfluten."
